summary: a zone over a counting parent takes a first block, then one twice as large when the newest is full, or just enough when the parent refuses that; it grows and shrinks only its newest allocation in place, moves any other, reports out_of_memory unchanged when the parent refuses every block, gives older blocks back at reset and keeps the newest, and gives every block back at release
